.TH FILEDIFFADVANCED 1
.SH NAME
filediffadvanced \- compare files and report performance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filediffadvanced
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.I file1 file2
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compares regular files using read-only memory mappings. Missing trailing bytes count as differences. Reports elapsed byte comparison time and combined input throughput in MiB/s.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Show first 20 differing byte positions, zero-based; -1 denotes a missing byte.
.TP
.B \-t
Also compare corresponding lines, showing the first 20 differing line numbers and total count.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 identical or help; 1 different; 2 error or interruption.
.SH NOTES
Inputs must remain unchanged during comparison. Line comparison is positional. Timing excludes mapping setup and the optional line pass. SIGINT and SIGTERM request orderly cleanup.
